                                "sense_id": "c44293b2-a384-3004-be82-4e17948679ed",
                                "text": "Kalua was a man of unusual height and powerful build: in any fair, festival or mela, he could always be spotted towering above the crowd—even the jugglers on stilts were usually not so tall as he."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b2aef8b-b914-4fda-bd07-2d8613e92bbc",
                                "sense_id": "c44293b2-a384-3004-be82-4e17948679ed",
                                "text": "Every year there was a mela in the small village where Jutimala lived and Khitish would send three workers to set up a stall there."
                            }
                        ]
